(Geoffrey Rogers) writes:
>In general you can enchanted weapons to +6. If you are lucky you can get
>it higher, but you stand a good chance of your weapon vaporizing after +6.
>For armor it is +3. You can something find armor or weapons that have
>higher plus values, but when you do its all luck.

  Well, to be precise, it is safe to enchant a weapon so long as *before*
enchanting it is +5 or less.  It is safe to enchant a piece of armor so
long as before enchanting it is +3 or less.  There is an exception, 
though:  an elven mithril coat can safely be enchanted so long as it
is not higher than +5.  (A spoiler, but something absolutely impossible
to figure out on your own.)

